Package: harmony-server
Version: 0.0.0
Architecture: all
Maintainer: marthofdoom <marthofdoom@users.noreply.github.com>
Depends: python3 (>= 3.11), python3-venv, python3-pip, ffmpeg
Recommends: pipewire | pulseaudio-utils
Section: sound
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/marthofdoom/harmony
Description: Harmony music hub — headless server
 A federated, self-hosted music hub: an always-on HTTP API and mDNS mesh node
 that the desktop, web, and mobile clients talk to. This package runs Harmony
 headless as a systemd service (no GTK), installing the app into a private
 virtualenv under /opt/harmony.
 .
 For inter-instance audio routing you also need roc-toolkit (or the RTP
 fallback) and a PipeWire/PulseAudio stack on this host; the mesh, HTTP API,
 accounts, search, and streaming work without them.
